#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Quantum circuits are executed on IBM&reg; hardware as sequences of microwave pulses that need to be scheduled and run at precise time intervals.\n"
"Unfortunately, unwanted interactions between qubits can lead to coherent errors on idling qubits. Dynamical decoupling works by inserting pulse sequences on idling qubits to approximately cancel out the effect of these errors. Each inserted pulse sequence amounts to an identity operation, but the physical presence of the pulses has the effect of suppressing errors.\n"
"There are many possible choices of pulse sequences, and which sequence is better for each particular case remains an [active area of research](https://journals.aps.org/prapplied/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevApplied.20.064027).\n"
msgstr ""
"Litar kuantum dilaksanakan pada perkakasan IBM&reg; sebagai urutan nadi gelombang mikro yang perlu dijadualkan dan dijalankan pada selang masa yang tepat.\n"
"Malangnya, interaksi tidak diingini antara qubit boleh membawa kepada ralat koheren pada qubit yang melahu. Dynamical decoupling berfungsi dengan memasukkan urutan nadi pada qubit yang melahu untuk kira-kira membatalkan kesan ralat ini. Setiap urutan nadi yang dimasukkan setara dengan operasi identiti, tetapi kehadiran fizikal nadi tersebut mempunyai kesan menindas ralat.\n"
"Terdapat banyak pilihan urutan nadi yang mungkin, dan urutan mana yang lebih baik untuk setiap kes tertentu masih merupakan [bidang penyelidikan aktif](https://journals.aps.org/prapplied/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevApplied.20.064027).\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Note that dynamical decoupling is mainly useful for circuits containing gaps in which some qubits sit idle without any operations acting on them. If the operations in the circuit are packed very densely, such that all of the qubits are busy most of the time, then the addition of dynamical decoupling pulses might not improve performance. In fact, it could even worsen performance due to imperfections in the pulses themselves.\n"
msgstr "Perlu diingat bahawa dynamical decoupling terutamanya berguna untuk litar yang mengandungi jurang di mana sebahagian qubit duduk melahu tanpa sebarang operasi yang bertindak ke atasnya. Jika operasi dalam litar sangat padat, sedemikian rupa sehingga semua qubit sibuk sebahagian besar masa, maka penambahan nadi dynamical decoupling mungkin tidak meningkatkan prestasi. Malah, ia boleh memburukkan lagi prestasi akibat ketidaksempurnaan dalam nadi itu sendiri.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The diagram below depicts dynamical decoupling with an XX pulse sequence. The abstract circuit on the left is mapped onto a microwave pulse schedule on the top right. The bottom right depicts the same schedule, but with a sequence of two X pulses inserted during an idle period of the first qubit.\n"
msgstr "Rajah di bawah menggambarkan dynamical decoupling dengan urutan nadi XX. Litar abstrak di sebelah kiri dipetakan ke jadual nadi gelombang mikro di kanan atas. Kanan bawah menggambarkan jadual yang sama, tetapi dengan urutan dua nadi X yang dimasukkan semasa tempoh melahu qubit pertama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of dynamical decoupling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/dd.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran dynamical decoupling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/dd.avif)\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable dynamical decoupling the following ways:\n"
"    - The [Dynamical decoupling transpiler pass](/guides/dynamical-decoupling-pass-manager) in Qiskit\n"
"    - The dynamical decoupling option if using IBM Quantum [Estimator](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-estimator-options#dynamical_decoupling) or [Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-sampler-options#dynamical_decoupling)\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda boleh mendayakan dynamical decoupling dengan cara berikut:\n"
"    - [Laluan transpiler dynamical decoupling](/guides/dynamical-decoupling-pass-manager) dalam Qiskit\n"
"    - Pilihan dynamical decoupling jika menggunakan IBM Quantum [Estimator](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-estimator-options#dynamical_decoupling) atau [Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-sampler-options#dynamical_decoupling)\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"twirling\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"twirling\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling {#pauli-twirling}"
msgstr "Pauli twirling {#pauli-twirling}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirling, also known as [randomized compiling](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.94.052325), is a widely used technique for converting arbitrary noise channels into noise channels with more specific structure.\n"
msgstr "Twirling, juga dikenali sebagai [pengkompilan rawak](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.94.052325), adalah teknik yang digunakan secara meluas untuk menukar saluran hingar sewenang-wenangnya menjadi saluran hingar dengan struktur yang lebih spesifik.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling is a special kind of twirling that uses Pauli operations. It has the effect of transforming any quantum channel into a Pauli channel. Performed alone, it can mitigate coherent noise because coherent noise tends to accumulate quadratically with the number of operations, whereas Pauli noise accumulates linearly. Pauli twirling is often combined with other error mitigation techniques that work better with Pauli noise than with arbitrary noise.\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling adalah jenis twirling khas yang menggunakan operasi Pauli. Ia mempunyai kesan mengubah sebarang saluran kuantum menjadi saluran Pauli. Apabila dilakukan secara bersendirian, ia boleh mengurangkan hingar koheren kerana hingar koheren cenderung terkumpul secara kuadratik dengan bilangan operasi, sedangkan hingar Pauli terkumpul secara linear. Pauli twirling sering digabungkan dengan teknik mitigasi ralat lain yang berfungsi lebih baik dengan hingar Pauli berbanding hingar sewenang-wenangnya.\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Pauli twirling is implemented by sandwiching a chosen set of gates with randomly chosen single-qubit Pauli gates in such a way that the ideal effect of the gate remains the same. The result is that a single circuit is replaced with a random ensemble of circuits, all with the same ideal effect. When sampling the circuit, samples are drawn from multiple random instances, rather than just a single one.\n"
msgstr "Pauli twirling dilaksanakan dengan mengapit set gate yang dipilih dengan gate Pauli satu qubit yang dipilih secara rawak sedemikian rupa sehingga kesan ideal gate tetap sama. Hasilnya ialah satu litar digantikan dengan ensemble rawak litar, semua dengan kesan ideal yang sama. Apabila menyampel litar, sampel diambil dari pelbagai contoh rawak, bukan hanya satu.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of Pauli twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/pauli_twirling.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran Pauli twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/pauli_twirling.svg)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Since most of the errors in current quantum hardware come from two-qubit gates, this technique is often applied exclusively to (native) two-qubit gates. The following diagram depicts some Pauli twirls for the CNOT and ECR gates. Every circuit within a row has the same ideal effect.\n"
msgstr "Oleh kerana sebahagian besar ralat dalam perkakasan kuantum semasa datang dari gate dua qubit, teknik ini sering diterapkan secara eksklusif pada gate dua qubit (asli). Rajah berikut menggambarkan beberapa Pauli twirl untuk gate CNOT dan ECR. Setiap litar dalam satu baris mempunyai kesan ideal yang sama.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of gate twirls](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/gate_twirls.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran twirl gate](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/gate_twirls.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-10-13 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable Pauli twirling the following ways:\n"
"    - A [Pauli twirling custom pass](/guides/custom-transpiler-pass) in Qiskit\n"
"    - The twirling options if using IBM Quantum [Estimator](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-estimator-options#twirling) or [Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-sampler-options#twirling)\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda boleh mendayakan Pauli twirling dengan cara berikut:\n"
"    - [Laluan tersuai Pauli twirling](/guides/custom-transpiler-pass) dalam Qiskit\n"
"    - Pilihan twirling jika menggunakan IBM Quantum [Estimator](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-estimator-options#twirling) atau [Sampler](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-sampler-options#twirling)\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"trex\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"trex\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX) {#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex}"
msgstr "Pemadaman Ralat Readout yang di-Twirl (TREX) {#twirled-readout-error-extinction-trex}"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"[Twirled Readout Error eXtinction (TREX)](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.105.032620) mitigates the effect of measurement errors for the estimation of Pauli observable expectation values.\n"
"It is based on the notion of twirled measurements, which are accomplished by randomly substituting measurement gates by a sequence of (1) a Pauli X gate, (2) a measurement, and (3) classical bit flip. Just like in standard gate twirling, this sequence is equivalent to a plain measurement in the absence of noise, as depicted in the following diagram:\n"
msgstr ""
"[Pemadaman Ralat Readout yang di-Twirl (TREX)](https://journals.aps.org/pra/abstract/10.1103/PhysRevA.105.032620) mengurangkan kesan ralat pengukuran untuk anggaran nilai jangkaan boleh cerap Pauli.\n"
"Ia berdasarkan konsep pengukuran yang di-twirl, yang dicapai dengan menggantikan gate pengukuran secara rawak dengan urutan (1) gate Pauli X, (2) pengukuran, dan (3) pembalikan bit klasik. Sama seperti dalam twirling gate standard, urutan ini setara dengan pengukuran biasa tanpa adanya hingar, seperti yang digambarkan dalam rajah berikut:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of measurement twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/measurement_twirling.svg)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran pengukuran twirling](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/measurement_twirling.svg)\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In the presence of readout error, measurement twirling has the effect of diagonalizing the readout-error transfer matrix, making it easy to invert. A rescaling term from the diagonal noise channel is learned by\n"
"benchmarking random circuits initialized in the zero state. This allows\n"
"the service to remove bias from expectation values that result from\n"
"readout noise. Estimating the readout-error transfer matrix requires executing additional calibration circuits, which introduces a small overhead.\n"
msgstr "Dalam kehadiran ralat readout, twirling pengukuran mempunyai kesan mendiagonalkan matriks pemindahan ralat readout, menjadikannya mudah untuk disongsangkan. Sebutan penskalan semula dari saluran hingar pepenjuru dipelajari dengan menanda aras (benchmarking) litar rawak yang dimulakan dalam keadaan sifar. Ini membolehkan perkhidmatan mengeluarkan berat sebelah daripada nilai jangkaan yang terhasil daripada hingar readout. Menganggar matriks pemindahan ralat readout memerlukan melaksanakan litar kalibrasi tambahan, yang memperkenalkan sedikit overhead.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable TREX the following ways:\n"
"    - The [Qiskit Mitigation](/addons/qiskit-mitigation) addon for Qiskit\n"
"    - The [`measure_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#measure_mitigation) if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
"    - The [resilience level](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda boleh mendayakan TREX dengan cara berikut:\n"
"    - Addon [Qiskit Mitigation](/addons/qiskit-mitigation) untuk Qiskit\n"
"    - [Pilihan `measure_mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#measure_mitigation) jika menggunakan IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
"    - [Tahap ketahanan](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) jika menggunakan IBM Quantum Estimator\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"zne\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"zne\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) {#zero-noise-extrapolation-zne}"
msgstr "Ekstrapolasi sifar-hingar (ZNE) {#zero-noise-extrapolation-zne}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Zero-noise extrapolation (ZNE) is a technique for mitigating errors in estimating expectation values of observables. While it often improves results, it is not guaranteed to produce an unbiased result.\n"
msgstr "Ekstrapolasi sifar-hingar (ZNE) adalah teknik untuk mengurangkan ralat dalam menganggar nilai jangkaan boleh cerap. Walaupun ia sering meningkatkan keputusan, ia tidak dijamin menghasilkan keputusan yang tidak berat sebelah.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE consists of two stages:\n"
msgstr "ZNE terdiri daripada dua peringkat:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Noise amplification_: The original quantum circuit is executed multiple times at different noise rates. (This can be done with either gate folding or [probabilistic error amplification](#pea).)\n"
msgstr "_Amplifikasi hingar_: Litar kuantum asal dilaksanakan beberapa kali pada kadar hingar yang berbeza. (Ini boleh dilakukan sama ada dengan gate folding atau [amplifikasi ralat kebarangkalian](#pea).)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "_Extrapolation_: The ideal result is estimated by extrapolating the noisy expectation value results to the zero-noise limit. (Typically with either an exponential or polynomial.)\n"
msgstr "_Ekstrapolasi_: Keputusan ideal dianggar dengan mengekstrapolasi keputusan nilai jangkaan berhingar ke had sifar-hingar. (Lazimnya dengan sama ada eksponen atau polinomial.)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Both the noise amplification and extrapolation stages can be implemented in many different ways. By default, IBM Quantum Compute implements noise amplification by \"digital gate folding,\" which means that two-qubit gates are replaced with equivalent sequences of the gate and its inverse. For example, replacing a unitary $U$ with $U U^\\dagger U$ would yield a noise amplification factor of 3. For the extrapolation, you can choose from one of several functional forms, including a linear fit or an exponential fit.\n"
"The image below depicts digital gate folding on the left, and the extrapolation procedure on the right.\n"
msgstr ""
"Kedua-dua peringkat amplifikasi hingar dan ekstrapolasi boleh dilaksanakan dalam pelbagai cara yang berbeza. Secara lalai, IBM Quantum Compute melaksanakan amplifikasi hingar melalui \"pelipatan gate digital,\" yang bermakna gate dua qubit digantikan dengan urutan setara gate tersebut dan inversnya. Contohnya, menggantikan uniter $U$ dengan $U U^\\dagger U$ akan menghasilkan faktor amplifikasi hingar sebanyak 3. Untuk ekstrapolasi, anda boleh memilih dari salah satu daripada beberapa bentuk fungsian, termasuk padanan linear atau padanan eksponen.\n"
"Imej di bawah menggambarkan pelipatan gate digital di sebelah kiri, dan prosedur ekstrapolasi di sebelah kanan.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Depiction of ZNE](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/zne.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Gambaran ZNE](/docs/images/guides/error-mitigation-explanation/zne.avif)\n"

# doq: fixed after review 2026-09-29 · verified 2026-10-18
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The overhead of this method scales with the number of noise factors. The\n"
"default settings sample the expectation value at three noise factors,\n"
"leading to a roughly 3x overhead.\n"
msgstr "Overhead kaedah ini berskala dengan bilangan faktor hingar. Tetapan lalai menyampel nilai jangkaan pada tiga faktor hingar, menghasilkan overhead kira-kira 3x.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable ZNE the following ways:\n"
"    - The [Qiskit Mitigation](/addons/qiskit-mitigation) addon for Qiskit\n"
"    - The [`zne_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#zne_mitigation) if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
"    - The [resilience level](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda boleh mendayakan ZNE dengan cara berikut:\n"
"    - Addon [Qiskit Mitigation](/addons/qiskit-mitigation) untuk Qiskit\n"
"    - [Pilihan `zne_mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#zne_mitigation) jika menggunakan IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
"    - [Tahap ketahanan](/guides/estimator-noise-management#resilience) jika menggunakan IBM Quantum Estimator\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"pea\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"pea\"></span>\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "ZNE with Probabilistic Error Amplification (PEA) {#zne-with-probabilistic-error-amplification-pea}"
msgstr "ZNE dengan Probabilistic Error Amplification (PEA) {#zne-with-probabilistic-error-amplification-pea}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "One of the main challenges in ZNE is to accurately amplify the noise affecting the target circuit. Gate folding provides an easy way to perform this amplification, but is potentially inaccurate and might lead to incorrect results.  See the article [\"Scalable error mitigation for noisy quantum circuits produces competitive expectation values\"](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2108.09197), and specifically page 4 of the supplementary information for details. Probabilistic error amplification provides a more accurate approach to error amplification through noise learning.\n"
msgstr "Salah satu cabaran utama dalam ZNE ialah mengamplifikasi hingar yang mempengaruhi litar sasaran secara tepat. Pelipatan gate menyediakan cara mudah untuk melakukan amplifikasi ini, tetapi berpotensi tidak tepat dan mungkin membawa kepada keputusan yang salah. Lihat artikel [\"Scalable error mitigation for noisy quantum circuits produces competitive expectation values\"](https://arxiv.org/pdf/2108.09197), dan khususnya halaman 4 maklumat tambahan untuk butiran. Amplifikasi ralat kebarangkalian menyediakan pendekatan yang lebih tepat untuk amplifikasi ralat melalui pembelajaran hingar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "PEA is a more sophisticated technique that performs preliminary experiments to reconstruct the noise and then uses this information to perform an accurate amplification. It starts by learning the twirled noise model of each layer of entangling gates in the circuit before they are run. After the learning phase, the circuits are executed at each noise factor, where every entangling layer of the circuits is amplified by probabilistically injecting single-qubit noise proportional to the corresponding learned noise model. See the article [\"Evidence for the utility of quantum computing before fault tolerance\"](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06096-3) for more details.\n"
msgstr "PEA adalah teknik yang lebih canggih yang melakukan eksperimen awal untuk merekonstruksi hingar dan kemudian menggunakan maklumat ini untuk melakukan amplifikasi yang tepat. Ia bermula dengan mempelajari model hingar yang di-twirl setiap lapisan gate pembelit dalam litar sebelum dijalankan. Selepas fasa pembelajaran, litar dilaksanakan pada setiap faktor hingar, di mana setiap lapisan pembelit litar diamplifikasi dengan menyuntik hingar satu qubit secara kebarangkalian berkadar dengan model hingar yang dipelajari. Lihat artikel [\"Evidence for the utility of quantum computing before fault tolerance\"](https://www.nature.com/articles/s41586-023-06096-3) untuk butiran lanjut.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"PEA consists of three stages:\n"
"1. _Learning_: The twirled noise model of each layer of entangling gates in the circuit is learned.\n"
"1. _Noise amplification_: The original quantum circuit is executed multiple times at different noise factors.\n"
"2. _Extrapolation_: The ideal result is estimated by extrapolating the noisy expectation value results to the zero-noise limit.\n"
msgstr ""
"PEA terdiri daripada tiga peringkat:\n"
"1. _Pembelajaran_: Model hingar yang di-twirl setiap lapisan gate pembelit dalam litar dipelajari.\n"
"1. _Amplifikasi hingar_: Litar kuantum asal dilaksanakan beberapa kali pada faktor hingar yang berbeza.\n"
"2. _Ekstrapolasi_: Keputusan ideal dianggar dengan mengekstrapolasi keputusan nilai jangkaan berhingar ke had sifar-hingar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For utility-scale experiments, PEA is often the best choice.\n"
msgstr "Untuk eksperimen skala utiliti, PEA sering menjadi pilihan terbaik.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Because PEA is a ZNE noise amplification technique, you also need to enable ZNE. You can enable PEA and ZNE  the following ways:\n"
"    - The [Qiskit Mitigation](/addons/qiskit-mitigation) addon for Qiskit\n"
"    - The [`zne_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#zne_mitigation) with [`pea`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-zne-options#amplifier) as the amplifier if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
msgstr ""
"Oleh sebab PEA ialah teknik amplifikasi hingar ZNE, anda juga perlu mendayakan ZNE. Anda boleh mendayakan PEA dan ZNE dengan cara berikut:\n"
"    - Addon [Qiskit Mitigation](/addons/qiskit-mitigation) untuk Qiskit\n"
"    - [Pilihan `zne_mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#zne_mitigation) dengan [`pea`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-zne-options#amplifier) sebagai penguat jika menggunakan IBM Quantum Estimator\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Noise learning required\">\n"
"If you are using the new client-side Estimator introduced in `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, a separate noise-learning job is required to use PEA.\n"
"See [Migrate from server-side to client-side Sampler and Estimator](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) for more information.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Pembelajaran hingar diperlukan\">\n"
"Jika anda menggunakan Estimator sisi klien baharu yang diperkenalkan dalam `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, kerja pembelajaran hingar yang berasingan diperlukan untuk menggunakan PEA.\n"
"Lihat [Migrasi daripada Sampler dan Estimator sisi pelayan ke sisi klien](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) untuk maklumat lanjut.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "<span id=\"pec\"></span>\n"
msgstr "<span id=\"pec\"></span>\n"

#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) {#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec}"
msgstr "Pembatalan ralat kebarangkalian (PEC) {#probabilistic-error-cancellation-pec}"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Probabilistic error cancellation (PEC) is a technique for mitigating errors in estimating expectation values of observables. Unlike ZNE, it returns an unbiased estimate of the expectation value. However, it generally incurs a greater overhead.\n"
msgstr "Pembatalan ralat kebarangkalian (PEC) adalah teknik untuk mengurangkan ralat dalam menganggar nilai jangkaan boleh cerap. Tidak seperti ZNE, ia mengembalikan anggaran yang tidak berat sebelah bagi nilai jangkaan. Namun, ia umumnya menanggung overhead yang lebih besar.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In PEC, the effect of an ideal target circuit is expressed as a linear combination of noisy circuits that are actually implementable in practice:\n"
msgstr "Dalam PEC, kesan litar sasaran ideal dinyatakan sebagai gabungan linear litar berhingar yang sebenarnya boleh dilaksanakan dalam amalan:\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{O}_{\\text{ideal}} = \\sum_{i} \\eta_i \\mathcal{O}_{noisy, i}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\mathcal{O}_{\\text{ideal}} = \\sum_{i} \\eta_i \\mathcal{O}_{noisy, i}\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The output of the ideal circuit can then be reproduced by executing different noisy circuit instances drawn from a random ensemble defined by the linear combination. If the coefficients $\\eta_i$ form a probability distribution, they can be used directly as the probabilities of the ensemble. In practice, some of the coefficients are negative, so they form a quasi-probability distribution instead. They can still be used to define a random ensemble, but there is a sampling overhead related to the negativity of the quasi-probability distribution, which is characterized by the quantity\n"
msgstr "Output litar ideal kemudian boleh dihasilkan semula dengan melaksanakan contoh litar berhingar yang berbeza yang diambil dari ensemble rawak yang ditakrifkan oleh gabungan linear. Jika pekali $\\eta_i$ membentuk taburan kebarangkalian, ia boleh digunakan terus sebagai kebarangkalian ensemble. Dalam amalan, sesetengah pekali adalah negatif, jadi ia membentuk taburan quasi-kebarangkalian. Ia masih boleh digunakan untuk menakrifkan ensemble rawak, tetapi terdapat overhead pensampelan yang berkaitan dengan kenegatifan taburan quasi-kebarangkalian, yang dicirikan oleh kuantiti\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\gamma = \\sum_{i} \\lvert \\eta_i \\rvert \\geq 1.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\gamma = \\sum_{i} \\lvert \\eta_i \\rvert \\geq 1.\n"
"$$\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The sampling overhead is a multiplicative factor on the number of shots required to estimate an expectation value to a given precision, compared to the number of shots that would be needed from the ideal circuit. It scales quadratically with $\\gamma$, which in turn scales exponentially with the depth of the circuit.\n"
msgstr "Overhead pensampelan adalah faktor pendarab pada bilangan shot yang diperlukan untuk menganggar nilai jangkaan kepada ketepatan tertentu, berbanding bilangan shot yang diperlukan dari litar ideal. Ia berskala secara kuadratik dengan $\\gamma$, yang seterusnya berskala secara eksponen dengan kedalaman litar.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"You can enable PEC  the following ways:\n"
"    - The [Qiskit Mitigation](/addons/qiskit-mitigation) addon for Qiskit\n"
"    - The [`pec_mitigation` option](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#pec_mitigation) if using IBM Quantum Estimator\n"
msgstr ""
"Anda boleh mendayakan PEC dengan cara berikut:\n"
"    - Addon [Qiskit Mitigation](/addons/qiskit-mitigation) untuk Qiskit\n"
"    - [Pilihan `pec_mitigation`](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/qiskit-ibm-runtime/options-models-resilience-options#pec_mitigation) jika menggunakan IBM Quantum Estimator\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-09-28 · verified 2026-09-29
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Noise learning required\">\n"
"If you are using the new client-side Estimator introduced in `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, a separate noise-learning job is required to use PEC.\n"
"See [Migrate from server-side to client-side Sampler and Estimator](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) for more information.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"note\" title=\"Pembelajaran hingar diperlukan\">\n"
"Jika anda menggunakan Estimator sisi klien baharu yang diperkenalkan dalam `qiskit-ibm-runtime` v0.50.0, kerja pembelajaran hingar yang berasingan diperlukan untuk menggunakan PEC.\n"
"Lihat [Migrasi daripada Sampler dan Estimator sisi pelayan ke sisi klien](/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives) untuk maklumat lanjut.\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

